-- title:
--   Elliptic transport and Weil-constant identity at a scalar norm
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $K$ and $L$ are number fields with $L$ an extension of $K$ of degree $\operatorname{finrank}_K L = 2$ (hypothesis `h2`), $\sigma$ is a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$ (hypothesis `hgen`), $v$ is a nonzero prime of $\mathcal O_K$, and $K_v$ denotes the completion `v.adicCompletion K`, equipped with its valuation `Valued.v`. Write $E = L \otimes_K K_v$, write $\sigma$ also for the induced semilinear action `sigmaGL` on $\mathrm{GL}_2(E)$, and write $N(x) =$ `normString` $= \prod_{i<2} \sigma^{i}(x)$ for $x \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E)$ (the product in the order $x \cdot \sigma(x)$, the number of factors being $\operatorname{finrank}_K L$). For $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$, $\mathrm{Cent}(\gamma)$ denotes the centraliser of $\{\gamma\}$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ (`localCentralizer`), and for $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E)$, $T'_\delta$ denotes the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser [`AutomorphicForm.twistedCentralizer`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L220), i.e. the subgroup `sigmaCentralizer (sigmaGL K L (v.adicCompletion K) σ) δ` of $\mathrm{GL}_2(E)$; all these groups and $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$, $\mathrm{GL}_2(E)$ carry their Borel $\sigma$-algebras. An element $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(A)$ is called regular semisimple (`IsRegularSemisimple`) when $\operatorname{tr}(\gamma)^2 - 4\det(\gamma)$ is a unit; $y$ is a norm conjugator for $(\gamma,\delta)$ (`IsNormConjugator`) when `toTensorGL` $(\gamma) = y^{-1} N(\delta) y$, and $\gamma$ is a norm of $\delta$ (`IsNormOf`) when such a $y$ exists.
--
--   The data are: a unit $c \in K_v^\times$; an element $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E)$; the hypothesis `hδ` that the scalar matrix $c \cdot 1$ is a norm of $\delta$; the hypothesis `hδq` that for no unit $z$ of $E$ is the scalar matrix $z \cdot 1$ $\sigma$-conjugate to $\delta$, i.e. there is no $x \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E)$ with $z \cdot 1 = x^{-1}\delta\,\sigma(x)$; and a Haar measure $\tau'$ on $T'_\delta$ (hypothesis `hτ'`).
--
--   The assertion is the existence of elements $u_0, y_1 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E)$, an element $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$, a measure $\tau_S$ on the subgroup $S = T'_\delta \sqcap T'_{u_0\delta}$ and a measure $\tau_T$ on $\mathrm{Cent}(\gamma_0)$, subject to the following conjuncts.
--
--   (i) $u_0 \in T'_\delta$. (ii) $\gamma_0$ is regular semisimple. (iii) For every $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ the matrix $g^{-1}\gamma_0 g$ does not have both off-diagonal entries $(0,1)$ and $(1,0)$ equal to zero; that is, no conjugate of $\gamma_0$ is diagonal. (iv) $\gamma_0$ is a norm of $u_0\delta$. (v) $\tau_S$ is a Haar measure on $S$ and (vi) $\tau_T$ is a Haar measure on $\mathrm{Cent}(\gamma_0)$.
--
--   (vii) (Approximation with coupled measures.) For every neighbourhood $W$ of the scalar matrix $c \cdot 1$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ and every neighbourhood $V$ of $1$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(E)$ there is a $u \in V$ with $u \in S = T'_\delta \sqcap T'_{u_0\delta}$ such that $N(u\delta)$ is regular semisimple, and there is a $\gamma \in W$ with $\gamma \in \mathrm{Cent}(\gamma_0)$, $\gamma$ regular semisimple, and $y_1$ a norm conjugator for $(\gamma, u\delta)$, i.e. `toTensorGL`$(\gamma) = y_1^{-1} N(u\delta) y_1$; moreover there exist a measure $\tau_\gamma$ on $\mathrm{Cent}(\gamma)$ and a measure $\tau_u$ on $T'_{u\delta}$ such that: $\tau_\gamma$ and $\tau_u$ are Haar measures; the push-forward of $\tau_\gamma$ along the inclusion $\mathrm{Cent}(\gamma) \hookrightarrow \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ equals the push-forward of $\tau_T$ along $\mathrm{Cent}(\gamma_0) \hookrightarrow \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$; the push-forward of $\tau_u$ along $T'_{u\delta} \hookrightarrow \mathrm{GL}_2(E)$ equals the push-forward of $\tau_S$ along $S \hookrightarrow \mathrm{GL}_2(E)$; the pair $(\tau_\gamma,\tau_u)$ is coupled through $y_1$ in the sense of [`AutomorphicForm.Coupled`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L313), namely the push-forward of $\tau_u$ under $t \mapsto y_1^{-1} t y_1$ coincides, as a measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(E)$, with the push-forward of $\tau_\gamma$ under `toTensorGL`; and for every $\varphi_v : \mathrm{GL}_2(E) \to \mathbb{C}$ that is a semi-local test function (locally constant with compact support) there is a $J \in \mathbb{C}$ with [`AutomorphicForm.IsTwistedOrbitalIntegral K L v σ (u * δ) τu φv J`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L366), i.e. $J$ is a twisted orbital integral of $\varphi_v$ at $u\delta$ for $\tau_u$, taken with respect to the measure `semiLocalHaar K L v`.
--
--   (viii) (Volume identity for the Weil constant.) Let $\rho \in \mathbb{R}$ be such that $\int w \,\mathrm d\tau' = \rho$ for every $w : T'_\delta \to \mathbb{R}$ which is nonnegative, measurable, compactly supported and satisfies the normalisation $\int_{s \in S} w(s t)\,\mathrm d\tau_S = 1$ for every $t \in T'_\delta$ (here $s \in S$ is regarded as an element of $T'_\delta$ through the first inclusion of the infimum). Put
--   $$\theta = \bigl(\text{push-forward of } \tau_T\bigr)\{\,g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v) : g \in \mathrm{Cent}(\gamma_0),\ \mathrm v(\det g) = 1,\ \mathrm v(\operatorname{tr} g) \le 1\,\},$$
--   $$\Omega = \tau'\{\,t \in T'_\delta : \exists\, s \in K_v^\times,\ \mathrm v(s) = 1 \text{ and } \det t = \text{image of } s \text{ under } \mathrm{Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight}\,\},$$
--   both read as real numbers via `ENNReal.toReal`. Then: if there exists $t \in \mathrm{Cent}(\gamma_0)$ with $\mathrm v(\det t) = \mathrm{ofAdd}(-1)$, one has $\rho \cdot \theta = \Omega$; and if no such $t$ exists, one has $\rho \cdot \theta = 2\,\Omega$.
--
--   (ix) $\theta > 0$, i.e. the push-forward of $\tau_T$ gives strictly positive real mass to the set of $g \in \mathrm{Cent}(\gamma_0)$ with $\mathrm v(\det g) = 1$ and $\mathrm v(\operatorname{tr} g) \le 1$. (x) The $\tau'$-measure of the set of $t \in T'_\delta$ whose determinant is the image under `Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight` of a unit $s \in K_v^\times$ with $\mathrm v(s) = 1$ is finite (strictly less than $\top$).
--
--   This is the local package, at a finite place $v$ of $K$ and for a quadratic extension $L/K$, that transports a twisted conjugacy class of the second kind (no scalar matrix being $\sigma$-conjugate to $\delta$) to an elliptic regular semisimple class $\gamma_0$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$, provides coupled Haar measures on the corresponding centralisers together with existence of twisted orbital integrals, and records the resulting volume identity relating the Weil constant $\rho$ of $S \backslash T'_\delta$ to the $\tau'$-volume of the determinant-unit set. It is the transport-and-volume input to the comparison identifying the twisted orbital integral at $\delta$ with minus the orbital integral at the scalar $c \cdot 1$, and is obtained by combining the transport statement with the two volume computations it cites.
